# Hermes 0.21.5, built exactly as upstream prescribes: their git tag, their
# uv.lock, no overrides. Every finding below comes from pip's own vendored
# bundle or from the mcp package's own pin -- not from Hermes's dependency
# tree, which resolves clean on its own.
#
# Every remaining finding lives inside pip's vendored bundle
# (site-packages/pip/_vendor/), not in a package Hermes imports. Confirmed by
# reading a built image: the vendored msgpack/__init__.py declares (1, 1, 2),
# with pkg_resources beside it. Trivy files them under its aggregate "Python"
# target with no path in the report summary and no "(METADATA)" marker.
#
# Not fixable: the versions are frozen inside pip itself. Removing pip is
# unsafe because Hermes lazy-installs skill dependencies at runtime.
#
# Not reachable: all three require pip to talk to a package index. This
# container never runs pip at runtime, has no direct egress (internal=true
# network), and reaches every tool through the Trentina gateway.
#
#   HIGH    GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  msgpack 1.1.2      OOB read / crash on Unpacker reuse
#   HIGH    CVE-2025-47273       setuptools 70.3.0  path traversal in PackageIndex
#   MEDIUM  CVE-2026-59890       setuptools 83.0.0  MANIFEST.in exclusion bypass
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-59890

# anyio / httpcore2 / httpx2 — pinned by the `mcp` PyPI package's own extras
# metadata (mcp[...]'s dependency spec), not by hermes-agent or by anything
# in this Containerfile. Checked upstream's uv.lock at every tag from
# v2026.8.31 through v2026.9.24 (the one this image tracks): all still pin
# anyio==4.12.1, httpcore2==2.7.0, httpx2==2.7.0. No version of hermes-agent
# exists yet that resolves clean;
# this is blocked on the `mcp` package itself, upstream of upstream.
#
# Not reachable: same isolation as the entries above, more so per Scott
# (2026-09-20) — Kagetora sits behind Trentina and is not directly
# internet-reachable at all; an attacker would need the host or Trentina
# itself compromised first, at which point these three CVEs are moot.
#
#   CRITICAL  CVE-2026-63374  anyio 4.12.1       TLS cert spoofing via IDNA host encoding
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-84381  httpcore2 2.7.0    WebSocket traffic sent in plaintext via SOCKS5
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-84382  httpx2 2.7.0       DoS via streaming response decompression
CVE-2026-63374
CVE-2026-84381
CVE-2026-84382

# PyJWT / urllib3 -- disclosed after the 1.0.1 build, so they first blocked
# the gate on the bump to v2026.9.24. The bump does not introduce them:
# upstream's uv.lock pins PyJWT==2.13.0 and urllib3==2.7.0 at v2026.8.31, at
# v2026.9.24 and on main, and the image already in production carried both.
# Staying on the old tag would not have removed one of these findings; any
# rebuild of it fails the same gate.
#
# No upstream release fixes them yet. NousResearch/hermes-agent#128979 (bump
# PyJWT to 2.14.0) is open. Per this file's rule, the lockfile is not
# overridden here.
#
# Accepted by Scott (2026-10-01) on the same isolation as the entries above:
# no direct egress, every outbound call through the Trentina gateway. Where
# Hermes verifies a JWT, and whether any path uses an HTTPS proxy through
# urllib3, was not traced -- this is an acceptance of unchanged exposure, not
# a finding that the code is unreachable. Remove each entry when upstream's
# lockfile moves to PyJWT>=2.14.0 / urllib3>=2.8.0.
#
#   CRITICAL  CVE-2026-102268  PyJWT 2.13.0    (see advisory)
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-102266  PyJWT 2.13.0    auth bypass via empty HMAC key acceptance
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-102267  PyJWT 2.13.0    key substitution via unvalidated JWKS redirects
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-102271  PyJWT 2.13.0    auth bypass via DER public keys accepted as HMAC
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-102272  PyJWT 2.13.0    token forgery via Unicode byte-order mark handling
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-102273  PyJWT 2.13.0    token forgery via public JWK containers accepted as HMAC
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-97687   urllib3 2.7.0   traffic interception via HTTPS proxy TLS config override
#   HIGH      CVE-2026-97689   urllib3 2.7.0   DoS via unbounded allocation in chunk parser
CVE-2026-102268
CVE-2026-102266
CVE-2026-102267
CVE-2026-102271
CVE-2026-102272
CVE-2026-102273
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
